[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Caro-Kann Defence"]
[Variation "Classical Variation, 4...Nd7 5.Qe2 trap"]
[ECO "B17"]
[Character "tactical"]
[Risk "high"]
[EarlyMate "white"]
[Tricks "trap,smothered-mate"]
[For "black"]
[Kind "against-us"]
[Opponent "5.Qe2"]
[Start "1. e4 c6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 dxe4 4. Nxe4"]

4... Nd7 $6 { A sound move, but this course plays 4...Bf5. It lets White set a mating trap that beginners fall for. } 5. Qe2 { Looks like a quiet move. It aims the queen down the e-file at the e7 pawn, which now shields Black's king. } 5... Ngf6 $4 { Natural development, but it blocks the f6 square, so the king has no way out. } ( 5... Nb6 6. Nf3 Bf5 ) 6. Nd6# { Smothered mate: the king is boxed in by its own queen, bishop and knight, and the e7 pawn cannot take because it is pinned to the king by the queen. } *
